<title>USA: Cypress to redeem 3.15 pct convertible notes.</title>
<headline>Cypress to redeem 3.15 pct convertible notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cypress Semiconductor Corp on Tuesday called for redemption its 3.15 percent convertible subordinated notes due 2001.</p>
<p>About $110 million aggregate principal amount of the notes are outstanding. The total redemption price is about $99 million, the company said.</p>
<p>The redemption is effective March 26.</p>
<p>Cypress said note holders may convert the notes into Cypress common stock at 72.1746 shares per $1,000 principal at maturity, or may redeem the notes at $900.25 per $1,000 principal amount at maturity.</p>
</text>
